SWEET Bluetooth: boot-arg sweetbtpubscan=2 (patch 0232, ticket T-0936, W-BTSCAN), diagnostic knob, default off, =1 unchanged: also rewrites Own_Address_Type 0x01 -> 0x00 in bluetoothd's ACTIVE HCI_LE_Set_Scan_Parameters (0x200b, LE_Scan_Type 0x01). bt-up17 [obs, docs/reviews/T-9947-proof.md]: a client scan made bluetoothd send an active 0x200b with random own address and no 0x2005; Scan Enable answered 0x12 (Core v5.4 Vol 4 Part E s.7.8.11) and bluetoothd's scan-stopped handler (cbnz w1 at 0x100579910) exited 1. Cost: SCAN_REQ carries the controller public address on air (s.7.8.10); one BT GAP row per active rewrite; any other non-zero value of the boot-arg is a BT GAP row (was silently ignored).

